nit[\'Status\'] == \'Available\'\n        ]\n        \n        if not available_units:\n            continue\n            \n        # Calculate remaining resources for each unit\n        unit_scores = []\n        for unit_id in available_units:\n            unit = process_units[unit_id]\n            remaining_cpu = unit[\'CPU\'] - app[\'CPU Demand\']\n            remaining_memory = unit[\'Memory\'] - app[\'Memory Demand\']\n            remaining_storage = unit[\'Storage\'] - app[\'Storage\']\n            \n            # Score based on remaining resources (lower is better for best-fit)\n            score = remaining_cpu + remaining_memory + remaining_storage\n            unit_scores.append((unit_id, score))\n        \n        # Sort by score (best fit = least remaining resources)\n        unit_scores.sort(key=lambda x: x[1])\n        \n        # Allocate to best-fit unit\n        if unit_scores:\n            best_unit_id = unit_scores[0][0]\n            process_units[best_unit_id][\'Applications hosted (IDs)\'].append(app_id)\n            process_units[best_unit_id][\'Status\'] = \'Busy\'\n            allocations.append({\n                \'Application ID\': app_id,\n                \'Process Unit ID\': best_unit_id,\n                \'Remaining Resources\': {\n                    \'CPU\': remaining_cpu,\n                    \'Memory\': remaining_memory,\n                    \'Storage\': remaining_storage\n                }\n            })\n    \n    return allocations\n```\n\n## Recommendation\n\n**Apply `best_fit_allocation`** for this scenario because:\n\n1. ✅ **Works with current data** - Doesn\'t require future trajectory information\n2. ✅ **Efficient resource use** - Minimizes resource waste by filling units with least capacity\n3. ✅ **Appropriate for early steps** - Focuses on provisioning efficiency when visibility data is unavailable\n4. ✅ **Scalable** - Can handle multiple applications being allocated simultaneously\n\nThis approach will ensure that applica